# ==============================================================================
# Starter .gitignore — language-neutral defaults
#
# This list covers the things NO submission should ever commit: secrets,
# credentials, local environment files, and large or raw data. Add the
# ignore rules for your own language/toolchain below the marked section.
#
# GitHub maintains ready-made .gitignore files for most languages at
# https://github.com/github/gitignore — copy the one(s) you need into the
# "Language-specific" section.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Secrets and credentials (NEVER commit these) -----------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets.*
*.secret

# --- Local environment / OS ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp
*.log

# --- Data (do not commit raw or large data; document how to fetch it) ---------
# Keep small sample data in data/sample/ and ignore everything else in data/.
data/*
!data/sample/
!data/README.md
*.csv
*.parquet
*.xlsx
*.sqlite
*.db

# --- Build / output artifacts -------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
*.bom
sbom.json
sbom.spdx.json
# ...except the submission SBOM, exported from GitHub's dependency graph (make sbom)
!docs/sbom/sbom.spdx.json

# ==============================================================================
# Language-specific — paste rules for your stack here
# (Python, Node, Go, R, Rust, etc.)
# ==============================================================================

# --- Python (uv manages .venv; nothing is installed into the system Python) --
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Node (web front-end under web/, from Phase 4) ----------------------------
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*

# --- Project exceptions -------------------------------------------------------
# The organizers' curated data provider list is tracked despite data/* above.
!data/DATA_SOURCES.md

# Fixtures and provenance manifests are tracked; raw data is not.
!data/sample/**
!data/manifests/
!data/manifests/**

# The template's build/ rule is for build artifacts; the pipeline package is source.
!src/hre/build/

# Engine outputs: results/ is the working folder (never committed). The web bundle
# web/public/results/ IS committed (decision 74): regenerate with `make results-all export`
# after any change to the engine, the register or the inputs; tests/test_bundle.py fails if stale.
/results/

# Page-count PDFs (scripts/count_pages.py); attach them to the submission, never commit
docs/pdf/
